{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For they are lively.</b> Expert as midwives — the Targum renders מְיַלְּדוֹת חַיָּתָא. And our Sages interpreted: they are compared to beasts of the field (Sotah 11), which need no midwives. And where are they compared to beasts? גּוּר אַרְיֵה, זְאֵב יִטְרָף (Genesis 49), בְּכוֹר שׁוֹרוֹ (Deuteronomy 33), אַיָּלָה שְׁלֻחָה (Genesis 49); and as for him who was not written [with a beast-comparison] — the verse has included them all: וַיְבָרֶךְ אוֹתָם (ibid.); and furthermore it is written: מָה אִמְּךָ לְבִיָּא (Ezekiel 19)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:09.267606238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}